Derivation fixed instance: D=2, L=2, K=2. Interpreted s as the frozen beta scale, v_pi_1 as the level-1 per-code stratum logits a_k (K=2), and the isolated fixed instance has no train graph so the spec's edge-less cohesion value rho=0.5 is used. Level-1 cost uses Poincare expmap0 with c=1 and beta=s: C_k = d_c(exp0(z),exp0(theta_1_k)) - s*(1-|0.5-sigmoid(v_pi_1[k])|). Hard level-1 index is argmin C (argmax of exp(-C/tau)); level 2 is Euclidean nearest on the residual and uses raw codewords. Loss is per-row squared reconstruction ||z - theta_1,k1 - theta_2,k2||^2. v_pi_2 is accepted as the inert level-2 table because levels >=2 are Euclidean/untouched.

{"symbols":["z0","z1","theta1_1_0","theta1_1_1","theta1_2_0","theta1_2_1","theta2_1_0","theta2_1_1","theta2_2_0","theta2_2_1","s","v_pi1_0","v_pi1_1","v_pi2_0","v_pi2_1"],"args":[{"name":"z","width":2},{"name":"theta_1_1","width":2},{"name":"theta_1_2","width":2},{"name":"theta_2_1","width":2},{"name":"theta_2_2","width":2},{"name":"s","scalar":1},{"name":"v_pi_1","width":2},{"name":"v_pi_2","width":2}],"statements":["nz = sqrt(z0**2 + z1**2 + 1e-12)","xz0 = tanh(nz/2)*z0/nz","xz1 = tanh(nz/2)*z1/nz","nt11 = sqrt(theta1_1_0**2 + theta1_1_1**2 + 1e-12)","y110 = tanh(nt11/2)*theta1_1_0/nt11","y111 = tanh(nt11/2)*theta1_1_1/nt11","nt12 = sqrt(theta1_2_0**2 + theta1_2_1**2 + 1e-12)","y120 = tanh(nt12/2)*theta1_2_0/nt12","y121 = tanh(nt12/2)*theta1_2_1/nt12","den1 = (1 - (xz0**2 + xz1**2))*(1 - (y110**2 + y111**2))","d1 = acosh(1 + 2*((xz0-y110)**2 + (xz1-y111)**2)/den1)","den2 = (1 - (xz0**2 + xz1**2))*(1 - (y120**2 + y121**2))","d2 = acosh(1 + 2*((xz0-y120)**2 + (xz1-y121)**2)/den2)","sk0 = 1/(1+exp(-v_pi1_0))","sk1 = 1/(1+exp(-v_pi1_1))","rho = 0.5","C1 = d1 - s*(1 - Abs(rho - sk0))","C2 = d2 - s*(1 - Abs(rho - sk1))","qa0 = Piecewise((theta1_1_0, C1 <= C2), (theta1_2_0, True))","qa1 = Piecewise((theta1_1_1, C1 <= C2), (theta1_2_1, True))","r0 = z0 - qa0","r1 = z1 - qa1","e21 = (r0 - theta2_1_0)**2 + (r1 - theta2_1_1)**2","e22 = (r0 - theta2_2_0)**2 + (r1 - theta2_2_1)**2","qb0 = Piecewise((theta2_1_0, e21 <= e22), (theta2_2_0, True))","qb1 = Piecewise((theta2_1_1, e21 <= e22), (theta2_2_1, True))","loss = (z0 - qa0 - qb0)**2 + (z1 - qa1 - qb1)**2"],"output":"loss","code":"import torch\n\ndef compute(z, theta_1_1, theta_1_2, theta_2_1, theta_2_2, s, v_pi_1, v_pi_2):\n    z = torch.as_tensor(z, dtype=torch.float32)\n    if z.dim() == 1:\n        z = z.unsqueeze(0)\n    B = z.shape[0]\n\n    def rowvec(v):\n        v = torch.as_tensor(v, dtype=torch.float32)\n        if v.dim() == 1:\n            v = v.unsqueeze(0)\n        if v.shape[0] == 1 and B != 1:\n            v = v.expand(B, -1)\n        return v\n\n    q11 = rowvec(theta_1_1)\n    q12 = rowvec(theta_1_2)\n    q21 = rowvec(theta_2_1)\n    q22 = rowvec(theta_2_2)\n    a = rowvec(v_pi_1)\n    s = torch.as_tensor(s, dtype=torch.float32)\n    eps = 1e-12\n\n    def expmap0(u):\n        n = torch.sqrt(torch.sum(u * u, dim=1, keepdim=True) + eps)\n        return torch.tanh(n / 2.0) * u / n\n\n    def hdist(x, y):\n        nx2 = torch.sum(x * x, dim=1)\n        ny2 = torch.sum(y * y, dim=1)\n        d2 = torch.sum((x - y) ** 2, dim=1)\n        den = (1.0 - nx2) * (1.0 - ny2)\n        arg = 1.0 + 2.0 * d2 / den.clamp_min(eps)\n        return torch.acosh(arg.clamp_min(1.0 + 1e-7))\n\n    x = expmap0(z)\n    y11 = expmap0(q11)\n    y12 = expmap0(q12)\n    d1 = hdist(x, y11)\n    d2 = hdist(x, y12)\n\n    sk = torch.sigmoid(a)\n    rho = torch.tensor(0.5, dtype=torch.float32, device=z.device)\n    C1 = d1 - s * (1.0 - torch.abs(rho - sk[:, 0]))\n    C2 = d2 - s * (1.0 - torch.abs(rho - sk[:, 1]))\n    C = torch.stack([C1, C2], dim=1)\n\n    k1 = torch.argmin(C, dim=1)\n    tau = 1.0\n    P = torch.softmax(-C / tau, dim=1)\n    onehot = torch.nn.functional.one_hot(k1, num_classes=2).to(z.dtype)\n    sel = onehot + P - P.detach()\n    q1 = sel[:, 0:1] * q11 + sel[:, 1:2] * q12\n\n    r = z - q1\n    e21 = torch.sum((r - q21) ** 2, dim=1)\n    e22 = torch.sum((r - q22) ** 2, dim=1)\n    k2 = torch.where(e21 <= e22, torch.zeros_like(e21, dtype=torch.long), torch.ones_like(e21, dtype=torch.long))\n

q2 = torch.where(k2[:, None] == 0, q21, q22)\n\n    return torch.sum((z - q1 - q2) ** 2, dim=1)\n","excluded":["the train-only graph preprocessor and cached per-item rho: the isolated fixed instance has no train graph, so the specification's edge-less value rho=0.5 is used","the balanced Sinkhorn column coupling and hard argmax/STE assignment: the per-row derivation uses the row-wise argmin of C; the code's STE selector has the same forward value as the hard selection and exists only to carry gradients","v_pi_2 is the level-2 table and is inert because levels 2 and 3 stay Euclidean and untouched","the frozen median m and beta calibration are absorbed into s, which carries the frozen beta scale directly"]}

